cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software

title: "Trust-Region vs Line Search for Unconstrained Optimization: A Fair-Cost Study on Ill-Conditioned, Non-Convex, and Indefinite-Hessian Problems"
version: "0.5.2"
date-released: "2026-10-31"

abstract: >
  Code and data accompanying the manuscript of the same title (under review).
  Six unconstrained optimization solvers, three trust-region subproblem
  solvers (Cauchy Point, Dogleg, Steihaug-CG) and three line-search methods
  (BFGS-Armijo, BFGS-Wolfe, Newton with Levenberg-Marquardt regularization),
  are compared on 156 distinct instances of 36 problems: ill-conditioned,
  non-convex, and with a Hessian indefinite at the starting point. Oracle
  costs count the distinct points at which each oracle is evaluated, and
  wall-clock times are measured. Includes the result files, unit tests, and
  the scripts that reproduce the tables and figures of the manuscript.

